# [[.Name]]

[[.Title]]: [[.Summary]]. Generated by kickhub from `[[.Template]]` v[[.Version]], target **[[.Target]]**.

## Layout

| Path | What it is |
|---|---|
| `internal/job/job.go` | `Run(ctx)`: your work goes here |
| `cmd/job` | Runs the job once and exits non-zero on failure |
[[ if eq .Target "aws" -]]
| `cmd/lambda` | Runs the job when the schedule fires |
| `infra/` | Lambda, EventBridge schedule and both roles |
[[- else if eq .Target "gcp" -]]
| `infra/` | Cloud Run job, Cloud Scheduler job, registry and service accounts |
[[- else -]]
| `docker-compose.yml` | The job as a container |
[[- end ]]
| `.kickhub.yaml` | Records the template, version and parameters used |

## Run it

```sh
make test
make run            # one execution, locally
```
[[ if eq .Target "aws" ]]
```sh
make infra-apply    # builds, deploys, schedule: [[.P.aws_schedule]]
make invoke         # run it now
aws logs tail "/aws/lambda/[[.Name]]" --since 5m
```

Lambda stops a run after 15 minutes. For longer work use the `batch-job` template.
[[ else if eq .Target "gcp" ]]
```sh
make infra-apply                      # registry and service accounts
gcloud auth configure-docker [[.P.gcp_region]]-docker.pkg.dev
make image REPO="$(terraform -chdir=infra output -raw image_repository)"
make infra-apply IMAGE_URI="$(terraform -chdir=infra output -raw image_repository):$(git rev-parse --short HEAD)"
make execute                          # run it now; schedule: [[.P.gcp_schedule]]
```

The first `infra-apply` runs without an image and skips the job and its schedule; the second creates them.
[[ end ]]
Keep `Run` safe to execute twice: schedulers retry and occasionally double-fire.
